# GUI live updates

## Soft navigation

- Soft-nav must not block painting the page payload on a rebuilt main-nav response. Highlight from cached nav / URL immediately; refresh nav JSON in the background.
- When diagnosing multi-second soft-nav, measure `GET /api/pages/...` and `GET /api/navigation/...` separately before blaming the GUI bundler, HMR, or host CPU. Use request-budget fields (`path`, `duration_ms`, `sql_queries`, `budget_miss`) from API logs and browser `framework:navigation-*` performance measures; ceilings live in `framework-request-budgets.mdc`.

## Intent prefetch

- Primary same-shell nav links (and any soft-navigable `<a href>`) may prefetch `GET /api/pages/<path>` on desktop hover/focus after a short debounce. Prefer shared document-level intent handlers so addon nav that uses normal anchors participates automatically.
- Prefetch is **single-flight** per path: a second hover must reuse the in-flight or ready entry, not open a duplicate request.
- Leaving the link before click aborts an in-flight speculative prefetch (or cancels the debounce). Navigating elsewhere aborts or ignores superseded prefetches; commit still follows keep-previous / epoch rules.
- Click must reuse a ready or in-flight prefetch when present; otherwise fall back to the normal page fetch.
- Prefetch must **not** retry-loop on 401/4xx/5xx. Record failure once; session errors surface through the existing page loader / bootstrap path. Clear the prefetch cache on session expiry.
- Prefer `startTransition` (or equivalent) when applying large page JSON so input stays responsive.

## Stale-while-revalidate (keep previous)

- Soft-nav to a same-shell app route must keep the previous page content visible until the new page payload commits. Acceptable UX: dim/opacity and a subtle “Updating…” / progress indicator. Do not flash an empty main content shell for the whole wait.
- Heavy sections may arrive after the page shell via `deferred_section` placeholders (skeleton → parallel section GETs → concrete section). A deferred fetch failure must show a section error only; never unmount the page shell or sibling sections.
- Realtime-driven page reloads that use coalesce must keep the last good component tree until the follow-up load commits; no empty flash between coalesced loads.
- List/grid client state must not reset to `[]` solely because a refresh started. Apply new data atomically (replace or merge per existing merge helpers) when the response commits.
- Abort or epoch-ignore stale page / list responses when a newer navigation or refresh supersedes them (network abort where practical).
- First cold load (no previous tree) may still show a skeleton or Loading panel.

## Realtime refresh thrash

- Burst matching `page_paths` must coalesce: finish the in-flight page load, then at most one follow-up if dirty. Prefer `createRealtimeRefreshScheduler` (or equivalent dirty-bit coalesce) over trailing debounce that aborts itself, and over faster polling.
- Coalesce alone does not fix high-churn operator or collaborative UIs. Prefer emitters with `page_paths=[]` and in-place `framework:event` patches (see `framework-realtime.mdc`).

## Push-first settle (poll is backup only)

- Async pending → settled gates (media display gates, job/run rows, similar in-flight rows) must complete from realtime: emit after persistence with a patchable `record` and `page_paths=[]` when a mounted handler applies in place. Clients apply that event immediately — do not wait for the next poll tick.
- Safety polls are backup for missed pushes only. Prefer `createPendingSettlePoll` in `framework/addons/system/gui/utils/pendingSettlePoll.js` (backoff from a multi-second initial delay, cap the max, jitter, pause while `document.hidden`, stop when no pending rows remain). Ban permanent ~1s `setInterval` hammers on live settle surfaces while connected and idle.
- While any row is still pending, omit `If-None-Match` against shared list revisions that may still cache pre-settle bodies (`conditionalGetHeaders({ etag, hasPending: true })`). Align with `framework-cache-contracts.mdc`.

## Concurrent fetches and merges

- Any surface that issues overlapping list or detail refreshes (settle hooks, polls, self-echo after POST) must epoch-gate applies: ignore responses older than the latest request.
- When the client applies an optimistic HTTP body and also listens for a self-emitted realtime delta with the same ids, merge by id — never naive-prepend or wholesale-replace in a way that doubles or drops rows. Prefer `mergeRecordsById` / `reconcileOptimisticEcho` in `framework/addons/system/gui/utils/mergeRecordsById.js` (or an equivalent id-keyed merge).
- Paginated / infinite lists: a first-page refresh must merge with retained older pages; never replace the full client list with only the newest page window.
- Refuse to apply incomplete aggregate fields (counts, totals) from a payload that omitted them; incomplete soft remounts must not stomp good client state.
- Keep local timers for expiring overlays or effects on absolute end timestamps that survive payload rehydrate; remounts must not extend expired effects via relative remaining-time fallbacks.

## Pending controls and optimistic mutation ack

- User-initiated mutations must show pending/busy on the **busy control** within one frame (`aria-busy`, disabled, spinner). Do not default to page-wide busy overlays that block the whole shell.
- When a mutation response returns affected record(s), apply them to local list/detail state via merge-by-id (or field patch) before/without waiting for soft remount.
- Mutation success/error flash or inline error must not depend on soft remount; dispatch flash from the mutation handler.
- Ban remount-as-ack for record-level mutations when an in-place handler exists: do not `framework:refresh-page` / non-empty `page_paths` solely to acknowledge POST/PATCH/DELETE of a row, attachment, toggle, rating, or status. Emit `page_paths=[]` with a patchable `record` and let mounted surfaces (and peers) apply via `framework:event`.
- Shared endpoint helpers (`completeEndpointAction`) may still refresh when structure must rebuild or when `refresh` is explicitly required; prefer `refresh: false` plus local apply for record mutations.

## Media elements

- Do not drive continuous media reload via React `src={url}` on every parent render when the URL is unchanged. Set media sources imperatively and skip no-ops.
- Grid / collection tiles: field-only patches (badges, counts, pending flags, titles) must not remount media when the tile id and media URLs are unchanged. Prefer a memoized media child (see `GridItem` / `mediaIdentity`) over remounting `Thumbnail` on every parent render. Keep React keys on stable domain ids.
- Large grids must bound mounted DOM with `useGridDomWindow` (or `GridSectionBody` windowing) above the DOM budget; pair with `useGridImageLoadRange` sticky visited indices when the full list is still mounted below that budget. Reserve tile geometry with `aspectRatio` (and `containIntrinsicSize` where used) before media loads to avoid CLS.
